      "math_academy_id": "q-1394",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "The vector $a$ has magnitude $3$, the vector $b$ has magnitude $6$, the angle between $a$ and $b$ is ${30}^{∘}$ and $n$ is the unit vector that points in the direction of $a\\times b.$ Find $a\\times b$ in terms of $n.$",
      "worked_solution": "We use the formula for the cross product and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|a|\\cdot |b|\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot n \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\cdot n \\\\  & =18\\cdot 0.5\\cdot n \\\\  & =9n.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
